Z||000004||rider||12-01-2000||10:01 AM||||Thanks Guys,<BR>Now, what should a 88GT in great condition low miles well equiped go for?????||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||12-01-2000||10:19 AM||||Check the mall. There's at least one for sale, there. For a nice GT, expect to pay some $$$. <BR>Occasionally you'll find one for cheap, but they're rare. <BR>The real answer is that it will go for whatever someone is willing to pay. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||ChadMan||12-01-2000||10:48 AM||||An 88 GT, in great condition, with low miles will run you $6000-$8000.  A comparable 86-87 GT would run $4000-$6000.  The extra $2k buys you much better brakes, moderately better ride and handling, and exclusivity.<P>If you're planning to use the car as a daily driver, I'd recommend going with the 86-87.  Take it from someone who uses an 88 Coupe as a daily driver - 88 brakes and suspension parts aren't cheap and are sometimes hard to find.  86-87 parts are as close as your local AutoZone and are much cheaper.||||reg||1
